        "jsCode": "return [\n  {\n    \"input\": \"This is a comprehensive architectural description for AniStudio, a project designed to provide a cinematic and user-friendly anime and manga discovery platform.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## AniStudio: Project Architecture & UI/UX Description\\n\\n### 1. High-Level UX Explanation\\n\\nAniStudio aims to offer a **cinematic, immersive, and effortless anime discovery experience**. Users will navigate a clean, modern interface that prioritizes content. The platform leverages the Jikan API to provide a rich catalog of anime, with features like personalized watchlists, detailed show pages, and intelligent search. Smooth animations, thoughtful loading states, and responsive design ensure a delightful experience across all devices, making it easy for users to find their next favorite show.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Full Page-by-Page UI Description\\n\\n#### 2.1. Home Page\\n\\n*   **Purpose:** To welcome users, showcase trending and seasonal anime, and provide quick entry points to key features.\\n*   **Layout:**\\n    *   **Desktop/XL:** Hero section with a prominent featured anime (potentially with a parallax effect), followed by horizontally scrolling carousels for \\\"Trending Anime,\\\" \\\"Seasonal Anime,\\\" and \\\"Discover Something New\\\" (random suggestions).\\n    *   **Tablet:** Similar structure, but carousels might display fewer items at once. Hero section remains impactful.\\n    *   **Mobile:** Hero section is vertically optimized. Carousels are touch-swipeable, displaying 1-2 items at a time. Vertical stacking of sections for a fluid scroll.\\n*   **Content:**\\n    *   **Hero Section:** Large, high-quality background image/video of a featured anime. Title, brief synopsis, and a call-to-action button (e.g., \\\"Watch Trailer\\\" or \\\"View Details\\\").\\n    *   **Carousels:** Each carousel displays `ShowCard` components. Titles for each section (e.g., \\\"Top 25 Anime\\\").\\n    *   **Promotional Banners (Optional):** Subtle call-outs for new features or categories.\\n\\n#### 2.2. Browse Page\\n\\n*   **Purpose:** To allow users to explore the entire anime catalog with robust filtering and sorting capabilities.\\n*   **Layout:**\\n    *   **Desktop/XL:** A two-column layout. The left column houses the filter/sort controls. The right column displays a responsive grid of `ShowCard` components.\\n    *   **Tablet:** Filters may be condensed into a slide-out panel or a collapsible section above the grid. The grid of `ShowCard` components adjusts to fewer columns.\\n    *   **Mobile:** Filters are accessible via a dedicated button that opens a full-screen modal or a slide-up panel. The `ShowCard` components are displayed in a single, vertically scrolling column or a 2-column grid.\\n*   **Content:**\\n    *   **Filter/Sort Panel:**\\n        *   **Filters:** Dropdowns/Multi-select for Genre, Type, Year, Rating.\\n        *   **Sort:** Dropdowns for Popularity, Score, Alphabetical.\\n        *   **Search Bar (within Browse):** For refining results further.\\n    *   **Anime Grid:** A dynamic grid of `ShowCard` components. Pagination controls or infinite scroll mechanism at the bottom.\\n\\n#### 2.3. Show Details Page\\n\\n*   **Purpose:** To provide comprehensive information about a specific anime title.\\n*   **Layout:**\\n    *   **Desktop/XL:** A multi-section layout. A prominent hero area with the anime title, key image, and essential details. Below, sections for Synopsis, Episodes, Cast/Staff, Reviews, and Trailer.\\n    *   **Tablet:** Content sections might stack more vertically. Key details remain easily accessible.\\n    *   **Mobile:** A single, vertically scrolling column. Hero section is optimized for portrait view. Sections are clearly delineated.\\n*   **Content:**\\n    *   **Hero Section:** Large anime poster/key visual, title, year, episodes count, status, rating, genres (as clickable tags).\\n    *   **Synopsis:** Expandable text area.\\n    *   **Trailer:** Embedded video player (autoplay on hover for desktop).\\n    *   **Details Section:** Producers, studios, duration, source.\\n    *   **Cast & Staff:** Carousel or list of key personnel.\\n    *   **Reviews:** User reviews or aggregate scores.\\n    *   **Related Anime (Optional):** Carousel of similar shows.\\n    *   **Watchlist Button:** Prominently displayed for adding/removing from watchlist.\\n\\n#### 2.4. Search Page\\n\\n*   **Purpose:** To enable users to find anime using keywords, with live suggestions.\\n*   **Layout:**\\n    *   **Desktop/XL:** A large, central search input field. As the user types, a dropdown of search suggestions appears. Below, results are displayed in a grid of `ShowCard` components, similar to the Browse page.\\n    *   **Tablet:** Search bar is prominent. Suggestions appear below. Results grid adjusts.\\n    *   **Mobile:** Full-width search bar at the top. Suggestions overlay the content. Results are in a single or two-column grid.\\n*   **Content:**\\n    *   **Search Input:** With clear placeholder text and an icon.\\n    *   **Search Suggestions:** Dynamically updating list of anime titles matching the query. Clicking a suggestion navigates to the Show Details page.\\n    *   **Search Results:** A grid of `ShowCard` components populated as the user searches or after pressing Enter.\\n\\n#### 2.5. Profile Page\\n\\n*   **Purpose:** To display user information, watchlist, and potentially viewing history.\\n*   **Layout:**\\n    *   **Desktop/XL:** A structured layout with user avatar and details on one side, and a list/grid of their watchlist on the other.\\n    *   **Tablet:** Layout may adjust to stack sections vertically or use a condensed sidebar for watchlist.\\n    *   **Mobile:** A single column layout with user information at the top, followed by the watchlist.\\n*   **Content:**\\n    *   **User Information:** Avatar, username, join date, potentially stats.\\n    *   **Watchlist:** A browsable list/grid of `ShowCard` components, with options to remove or mark as complete.\\n    *   **Settings/Edit Profile (Optional):** Link to a separate settings page.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Component Architecture & Usage\\n\\n*   **Navbar (Global):**\\n    *   **Usage:** Persistently visible at the top. Shrinks on scroll.\\n    *   **Contains:** Logo, Global Search Input (with autocomplete), Quick Actions button (\\\"+ Add\\\"), Theme Toggle, Notifications Icon, Profile Menu (Avatar dropdown).\\n    *   **Sub-components:** Logo, SearchBarWithSuggestions, IconButton (Theme Toggle, Notifications), ProfileDropdown.\\n*   **Sidebar (Conditional Layout):**\\n    *   **Usage:** Appears on larger screens or as a collapsible panel. On mobile, triggered by a hamburger icon in the Navbar.\\n    *   **Contains:** Menu items (Home, Browse, Search, Watchlist, Profile), collapsible functionality, active state indicator, Logout button at the bottom.\\n    *   **Sub-components:** NavLink, IconButton.\\n*   **ShowCard:**\\n    *   **Usage:** Displays individual anime listings on Home, Browse, Search, and Profile pages.\\n    *   **Features:** Thumbnail image (lazy-loaded), title, score, genres, brief status. Hover effect to reveal more details or an \\\"Add to Watchlist\\\" button.\\n    *   **Micro-interactions:** Subtle hover scaling, light shadow movement.\\n    *   **Loading State:** Skeleton loader with shimmer effect.\\n*   **Carousel:**\\n    *   **Usage:** For horizontally displaying collections of `ShowCard` components (e.g., Trending Anime, Seasonal Anime).\\n    *   **Features:** Swipeable on touch devices, navigation arrows for desktop.\\n    *   **Animation:** Smooth transitions between slides.\\n*   **Footer (Global):**\\n    *   **Usage:** At the bottom of all pages.\\n    *   **Content:** Copyright info, links to About Us, Privacy Policy, Contact.\\n*   **FilterPanel/Sidebar (Browse Page):**\\n    *   **Usage:** Controls for filtering and sorting on the Browse page.\\n    *   **Components:** Dropdowns, multi-select checkboxes, sliders (for year/rating ranges).\\n*   **Pagination/InfiniteScroll:**\\n    *   **Usage:** To manage navigation through large lists of anime.\\n    *   **Implementation:** Standard pagination buttons or an intersection observer for infinite scroll.\\n*   **SkeletonLoader/Shimmer:**\\n    *   **Usage:** To provide visual feedback while data is being fetched, improving perceived performance. Applied to `ShowCard` thumbnails and key text elements.\\n*   **VideoPlayer:**\\n    *   **Usage:** For displaying anime trailers.\\n    *   **Features:** Autoplay on hover (desktop), mute toggle.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Layout Behavior for Each Breakpoint\\n\\n| Breakpoint    | Description                                                                | Layout Strategy                                                                                                     |\\n| :------------ | :------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\\n| **Mobile (≤480px)** | Touch-first, single-column focus.                                          | Vertical stacking of sections. `Navbar` hamburger menu for `Sidebar`. `ShowCard` in 1-2 columns. Swipeable carousels. |\\n| **Tablet (481–1024px)** | Balanced responsiveness, mixed layouts.                                    | `Navbar` with horizontal elements. `Sidebar` might be collapsible. Grid layouts for `ShowCard` (2-3 columns).        |\\n| **Desktop (1025–1439px)** | Full navigation and content density.                                       | Standard `Navbar` + `Sidebar`. Grid layouts for `ShowCard` (4-5 columns). Hover effects become more prominent.       |\\n| **Desktop XL (1440px+)** | Enhanced visual space, deeper interactions.                                | Max-width content, larger spacing. Potential for parallax effects in hero sections. Wider `ShowCard` grids.        |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. GSAP Animation Mapping\\n\\n*   **Page Load Animations:**\\n    *   **Stepper Sequence Reveal:** Sections and `ShowCard` components fade and slide in sequentially as the page loads.\\n    *   **Smooth Fade + Slide-Down:** Initial page load with a subtle fade-in and a slight downward slide.\\n    *   **Navbar Shrink on Scroll:** `Navbar` height and padding decrease with a smooth animation as the user scrolls down.\\n*   **Page Transition Animations:**\\n    *   **Fade + Slide Between Pages:** When navigating between pages, the outgoing page fades out and slides up, while the incoming page fades in and slides down.\\n    *   **Optional Parallax Hero:** For specific hero sections on pages like Home or Show Details, the background image moves at a different pace than the foreground content during scroll.\\n*   **Scroll-Triggered Animations:**\\n    *   **Cards Stagger from Bottom:** On pages with grids of `ShowCard` components, each card animates in from the bottom with a slight stagger effect as it enters the viewport.\\n    *   **Rows Fade One by One:** For sections with multiple horizontal rows of content, each row fades in and lifts slightly as it scrolls into view.\\n    *   **Section Lift-in Effect:** Larger content blocks (like synopsis or details on Show Details page) lift and fade into view as the user scrolls down.\\n*   **Micro Interactions:**\\n    *   **Hover Scaling:** `ShowCard` components subtly scale up on hover. Buttons have a slight press-down effect.\\n    *   **Button Press Feedback:** Buttons provide visual feedback (slight scale or color change) on click/tap.\\n    *   **Card Info Overlay:** On hover for `ShowCard`, additional info might smoothly overlay or animate into view.\\n    *   **Light Shadow Movement:** A subtle, dynamic shadow effect that follows the cursor on interactive elements, enhancing the \\\"cinematic\\\" feel.\\n*   **Reduced Motion Mode:** All animations will be disabled or significantly simplified (e.g., basic fades) when the user's system preference for reduced motion is detected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 6. MVC Mapping for Every Page\\n\\n#### 6.1. Home Page\\n\\n*   **Model:**\\n    *   `apiService.js`: Functions to fetch trending, seasonal, and random anime from Jikan API (`/top/anime`, `/seasons/now`, `/random/anime`).\\n    *   `stateStore.js` (e.g., Zustand/Redux): Stores fetched anime data, loading states, error states.\\n*   **View:**\\n    *   `HomePage.jsx`: Renders the layout, Hero section, and Carousels.\\n    *   `HeroSection.jsx`: Displays featured anime banner.\\n    *   `Carousel.jsx`: Renders `ShowCard` components in a scrollable list.\\n*   **Controller:**\\n    *   `useHomePageController.js`: Hooks to manage fetching data (calling `apiService`), updating state (`stateStore`), and handling initial page load animations.\\n\\n#### 6.2. Browse Page\\n\\n*   **Model:**\\n    *   `apiService.js`: Functions to fetch anime based on filters (`/anime?genre={...}&type={...}&page={...}`).\\n    *   `stateStore.js`: Stores fetched anime data, pagination info, current filters, sort order, loading/error states.\\n*   **View:**\\n    *   `BrowsePage.jsx`: Renders the filter panel and the grid of `ShowCard` components.\\n    *   `FilterPanel.jsx`: Contains filter/sort UI elements.\\n    *   `AnimeGrid.jsx`: Renders `ShowCard` components dynamically based on fetched data.\\n    *   `Pagination.jsx` or `InfiniteScroll.jsx`.\\n*   **Controller:**\\n    *   `useBrowsePageController.js`: Manages fetching data based on selected filters/sort, handles pagination/infinite scroll logic, updates state, and manages filter UI interactions.\\n\\n#### 6.3. Show Details Page\\n\\n*   **Model:**\\n    *   `apiService.js`: Functions to fetch specific anime details (`/anime/{id}`), characters (`/anime/{id}/characters`).\\n    *   `stateStore.js`: Stores fetched anime details, character data, trailer URL, loading/error states. Also manages watchlist state.\\n*   **View:**\\n    *   `ShowDetailsPage.jsx`: Renders the overall page structure, hero details, synopsis, trailer, etc.\\n    *   `AnimeDetailsHero.jsx`: Displays title, image, key stats.\\n    *   `SynopsisSection.jsx`: Renders synopsis text.\\n    *   `TrailerSection.jsx`: Embeds the video player.\\n    *   `WatchlistButton.jsx`: Handles adding/removing from watchlist.\\n*   **Controller:**\\n    *   `useShowDetailsPageController.js`: Fetches anime details and related data, manages trailer playback, handles watchlist add/remove actions (optimistic UI), and controls animations.\\n\\n#### 6.4. Search Page\\n\\n*   **Model:**\\n    *   `apiService.js`: Functions for search queries (`/anime?q={keyword}`) and for fetching search suggestions.\\n    *   `stateStore.js`: Stores search results, search suggestions, current query, loading/error states.\\n*   **View:**\\n    *   `SearchPage.jsx`: Renders the search input and the results grid.\\n    *   `SearchBarWithSuggestions.jsx`: Combines input field and suggestion dropdown.\\n    *   `SearchResultsGrid.jsx`: Displays `ShowCard` components.\\n*   **Controller:**\\n    *   `useSearchPageController.js`: Manages search input changes, triggers API calls for suggestions and results, updates state, handles navigation to Show Details from suggestions/results.\\n\\n#### 6.5. Profile Page\\n\\n*   **Model:**\\n    *   `apiService.js`: Functions to fetch user profile data (`/users/{username}`) and user's watchlist.\\n    *   `stateStore.js`: Stores user profile data, watchlist items, loading/error states.\\n*   **View:**\\n    *   `ProfilePage.jsx`: Renders user info section and the watchlist display.\\n    *   `UserInfoCard.jsx`: Displays avatar, username, etc.\\n    *   `WatchlistGrid.jsx`: Displays `ShowCard` components for the user's watchlist.\\n*   **Controller:**\\n    *   `useProfilePageController.js`: Fetches user data and watchlist, manages any actions on watchlist items (e.g., removal), and handles UI updates.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 7. Navigation Flow\\n\\n1.  **Landing on Home Page:** User sees featured content, can navigate via `Navbar` links (Home, Browse, Search, Watchlist, Profile) or `Sidebar` if expanded.\\n2.  **Browsing Anime:** From Home or Browse page, clicking a `ShowCard` navigates to `ShowDetailsPage`.\\n3.  **Searching Anime:** User types in the Global Search (Navbar) or Search Page. Suggestions appear; clicking a suggestion leads to `ShowDetailsPage`. Submitting a search on Search Page displays results grid, clicking a `ShowCard` leads to `ShowDetailsPage`.\\n4.  **Watchlist Management:** On `ShowDetailsPage`, clicking \\\"Add to Watchlist\\\" updates the user's watchlist. The Watchlist page displays these items, with options to remove.\\n5.  **Profile Access:** Clicking the Profile icon in the `Navbar` or `Sidebar` navigates to the `ProfilePage`.\\n6.  **Theme Toggle:** Toggles between light and dark modes with instant UI update.\\n7.  **Sidebar Toggle:** On mobile, clicking the hamburger icon toggles the `Sidebar` visibility. On larger screens, it might be permanently visible or collapsible.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 8. Color Palette + Typography\\n\\n*   **Visual Theme:** Cinematic, neutral colors with optional neumorphic/soft UI elements. Focus on content readability and a premium feel.\\n*   **Color Palette:**\\n    *   **Light Mode:**\\n        *   Primary Background: Off-white/light grey (`#F8F9FA`)\\n        *   Secondary Background/Cards: White (`#FFFFFF`)\\n        *   Primary Text: Dark Grey (`#212529`)\\n        *   Secondary Text: Muted Grey (`#6c757d`)\\n        *   Accent Color (Buttons, Links, Active States): A subtle, deep blue or teal (e.g., `#007bff` muted, or `#17a2b8`).\\n        *   Hover/Focus Shadow Color: Soft, desaturated blue/purple.\\n    *   **Dark Mode:**\\n        *   Primary Background: Deep charcoal/near black (`#121212`)\\n        *   Secondary Background/Cards: Dark grey (`#1E1E1E`)\\n        *   Primary Text: Light Grey/Off-white (`#E0E0E0`)\\n        *   Secondary Text: Muted dark grey (`#A0A0A0`)\\n        *   Accent Color: Brighter, saturated version of the light mode accent, or a more vibrant electric blue/cyan.\\n        *   Hover/Focus Shadow Color: Lighter, glowing version of the accent color.\\n*   **Typography:**\\n    *   **Headings:** Inter or Poppins (Bold, Semi-bold)\\n    *   **Body Text:** Roboto (Regular)\\n    *   **Font Sizes:** Responsive, with clear hierarchy. `h1` for page titles, `h2` for section titles, `body` for content.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 9. Accessibility + Reduced Motion Logic\\n\\n*   **Accessibility:**\\n    *   **Semantic HTML:** Use appropriate HTML tags for structure and meaning.\\n    *   **ARIA Attributes:** Implement ARIA roles and properties where necessary for screen reader users.\\n    *   **Keyboard Navigation:** Ensure all interactive elements are focusable and operable via keyboard.\\n    *   **Color Contrast:** Maintain sufficient color contrast ratios for text and interactive elements in both light and dark modes.\\n    *   **Focus Indicators:** Clear and visible focus outlines for interactive elements.\\n    *   **Alt Text:** Provide descriptive alt text for all meaningful images.\\n*   **Reduced Motion:**\\n    *   Detect `prefers-reduced-motion` media query.\\n    *   If `true`, disable all non-essential animations (e.g., card stagger, slide transitions, parallax effects). Fallback to simpler fades or no animation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 10. Performance (Lazy Load, Caching, Prefetch)\\n\\n*   **Lazy Loading Images:** Implement lazy loading for all `ShowCard` images and any other media that is not immediately in the viewport. This significantly speeds up initial page load times.\\n*   **Skeleton/Shimmer Loading:** Display skeleton loaders while data is being fetched for `ShowCard` components and other dynamic content sections. This provides immediate visual feedback.\\n*   **API Caching:** Implement client-side caching for frequently accessed API endpoints (e.g., trending anime, popular genres). This reduces redundant API calls.\\n*   **Prefetching:** On hover of a `ShowCard` or a navigation link, consider prefetching the associated API data for the target page to enable near-instant navigation.\\n*   **Code Splitting:** Use React's `lazy` and `Suspense` for route-based code splitting, ensuring users only download JavaScript for the pages they visit.\\n*   **Debouncing/Throttling:** For search input and scroll events, use debouncing and throttling to limit the number of API calls and expensive operations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 11. Micro-interactions and Icon Usage (Material UI Icons)\\n\\n*   **Material UI Icons:** Used extensively for navigation (Home, Search, Profile), actions (Notifications, Theme Toggle, Add), and within components. Examples:\\n    *   `HomeIcon`\\n    *   `SearchIcon`\\n    *   `AccountCircleIcon`\\n    *   `NotificationsIcon`\\n    *   `Brightness4Icon` (Theme Toggle)\\n    *   `AddIcon`\\n    *   `StarIcon` (Score indicator)\\n    *   `InfoOutlinedIcon` (Hover details)\\n*   **Micro-interactions:**\\n    *   **Hover Scaling:** `ShowCard` components and interactive buttons subtly scale up.\\n    *   **Button Press Feedback:** Buttons provide a tactile feedback on click/tap.\\n    *   **Card Info Overlay:** On hover, additional details on `ShowCard` smoothly animate into view.\\n    *   **Light Shadow Movement:** A subtle, dynamic shadow effect that follows the cursor on interactive elements, enhancing the \\\"cinematic\\\" feel.\\n    *   **Watchlist Toggle Feedback:** When adding/removing from the watchlist, a brief visual confirmation (e.g., icon change with a subtle animation) is displayed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 12. Skeleton/Loading States\\n\\n*   **`ShowCard` Skeleton:** Before actual anime data loads, `ShowCard` components will render as placeholders with a shimmering animation. This includes:\\n    *   A rectangular placeholder for the image.\\n    *   Line placeholders for the title and score/genre.\\n*   **Page-Level Skeleton:** For complex pages like Show Details, key sections (e.g., synopsis, trailer area) might show larger placeholder blocks with shimmering effects.\\n*   **Loading Spinners/Bars:** Used for critical loading states, such as initial page load or during filter application on the Browse page.\\n*   **Error States:** Graceful handling of API errors, displaying informative messages to the user with an option to retry.\\n\\n---\"\n  }\n]"
